# A Luxel library scene — Apache-2.0. Grammar: library/README.md.
# Scenery from loop tiles: kelp tiled along the floor (`fit tile`), one fish
# sprite used three times (flags 3 = flipped to swim the other way, `A` to
# de-sync their tails) and a bubble column that is a 6x16 tile rising forever.
# The kelp is rooted at row 64; on a 32-row panel only its tips sway into view,
# and the third fish and second bubble column live outside the 32x32 corner.
S - Aquarium
L pat 0 0 0 0 normal 100 none fill 1
N Water
I @pat/caustics
C sliderGroutPct 0
R 100 0:000814 90:00304f 180:0f7f99 255:a8f4ff
L pat 0 0 0 0 add 35 none fill 1
N Plankton
I @pat/twinkle
C sliderDensity 196608
R 100 0:000000 255:bff9ff
L sprite 0 24 64 40 normal 100 none tile 1
N Kelp
I @spr/seaweed
L sprite 26 0 6 64 normal 100 none tile 1
N Bubbles
I @spr/bubbles-tile
L sprite 51 0 6 64 normal 100 none tile 1
N Bubbles 2
I @spr/bubbles-tile
A 7
L sprite 4 6 0 0 normal 100 none fill 1
N Fish
I @spr/fish
L sprite 15 15 0 0 normal 100 none fill 3
N Fish 2
I @spr/fish
A 3
L sprite 38 34 0 0 normal 100 none fill 1
N Fish 3
I @spr/fish
A 5
